@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] accounts-stored-login-authority
User login tokens MUST be stored and their presence required for authentication.
Long-lived connections MUST consult current token presence and expiry instead of
relying only on a previously verified JWT signature.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] accounts-mail-secret-boundary
Magic-link email payloads MUST be encrypted at rest, absent from audit history and
job arguments, and excluded from diagnostics. User-facing magic-link requests MUST
NOT reveal recipient registration or provider/enqueue failure details.

Administrator audit projections MUST recheck current authority, remain keyset
bounded, and expose only redacted actor/target/action/time fields.
